§ `Article 2(3): areas outside Union law, and military, defence and national security`

-- Under Article 2(3), as a provider of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the matter outside the scope of Union law
-- 1 February 2025, Chapter I has not begun to apply, so nothing is covered (Art 113(a): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(3), as a provider of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the matter outside the scope of Union law` (Date 1 2 2025) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2 February 2025, the matter is outside Union law or a national security competence: JUST FALSE ("This Regulation does not apply to areas outside the scope of Union law")
-- MIRROR Art 2(3) first subparagraph: a provider and a deployer carrying out a task outside Union law
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(3), as a provider of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the matter outside the scope of Union law` (Date 2 2 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 2 February 2025, the matter is in neither: NOTHING (the sentence is silent about other matters)
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(3), as a provider of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the matter outside the scope of Union law` (Date 2 2 2025) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 27 July 2026, the text as amended: JUST FALSE (paragraph 3 was not changed)
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(3), as a provider of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the matter outside the scope of Union law` (Date 27 7 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under Article 2(3), as a provider of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the AI system used exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes
-- 1 February 2025, Chapter I has not begun to apply, so nothing is covered (Art 113(a): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(3), as a provider of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the AI system used exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes` (Date 1 2 2025) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2 February 2025, exclusively military, defence or national security: JUST FALSE ("This Regulation does not apply to AI systems where and in so far they are placed on the market, put into service, or used ... exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes")
-- MIRROR Art 2(3) second subparagraph: the same military AI system asked from each operator seat
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(3), as a provider of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the AI system used exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes` (Date 2 2 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 2 February 2025, a system with any other purpose too: NOTHING (limited by "exclusively")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(3), as a provider of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the AI system used exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes` (Date 2 2 2025) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 27 July 2026, the text as amended: JUST FALSE (the subparagraph was not changed)
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(3), as a provider of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the AI system used exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes` (Date 27 7 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under Article 2(3), as a provider of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the AI system not placed on the market in the Union whose output is used exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes
-- 1 February 2025, Chapter I has not begun to apply, so nothing is covered (Art 113(a): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(3), as a provider of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the AI system not placed on the market in the Union whose output is used exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes` (Date 1 2 2025) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2 February 2025, not placed or put into service in the Union and its output used in the Union exclusively for military purposes: JUST FALSE ("This Regulation does not apply to AI systems which are not placed on the market or put into service in the Union, where the output is used in the Union exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes")
-- MIRROR Art 2(3) third subparagraph: a provider and a deployer of an AI system outside the Union market whose output is military
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(3), as a provider of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the AI system not placed on the market in the Union whose output is used exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes` (Date 2 2 2025) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 2 February 2025, the output is also used for another purpose: NOTHING (limited by "exclusively")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(3), as a provider of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the AI system not placed on the market in the Union whose output is used exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes` (Date 2 2 2025) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2 February 2025, the system is placed on the market or put into service in the Union: NOTHING (the subparagraph speaks of systems not placed or put into service in the Union)
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(3), as a provider of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the AI system not placed on the market in the Union whose output is used exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes` (Date 2 2 2025) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 27 July 2026, the text as amended: JUST FALSE (the subparagraph was not changed)
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(3), as a provider of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the AI system not placed on the market in the Union whose output is used exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes` (Date 27 7 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE


§ `Article 2(5): the liability of providers of intermediary services`

-- Under Article 2(5), as a provider of an AI system, does the Regulation affect the application of the provisions on the liability of providers of intermediary services
-- 1 February 2025, Chapter I has not begun to apply, so nothing is covered (Art 113(a): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(5), as a provider of an AI system, does the Regulation affect the application of the provisions on the liability of providers of intermediary services` (Date 1 2 2025) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2 February 2025, a liability provision of Chapter II of Regulation (EU) 2022/2065: JUST FALSE ("This Regulation shall not affect the application of the provisions on the liability of providers of intermediary services")
-- MIRROR Art 2(5): a provider and a deployer that also provide an intermediary service
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(5), as a provider of an AI system, does the Regulation affect the application of the provisions on the liability of providers of intermediary services` (Date 2 2 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 2 February 2025, another provision: NOTHING (the sentence speaks of those provisions only)
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(5), as a provider of an AI system, does the Regulation affect the application of the provisions on the liability of providers of intermediary services` (Date 2 2 2025) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 27 July 2026, the text as amended: JUST FALSE (paragraph 5 was not changed)
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(5), as a provider of an AI system, does the Regulation affect the application of the provisions on the liability of providers of intermediary services` (Date 27 7 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE


§ `Article 2(6): AI systems and models developed for the sole purpose of scientific research and development`

-- Under Article 2(6), as a provider of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the AI system developed for the sole purpose of scientific research and development
-- 1 February 2025, Chapter I has not begun to apply, so nothing is covered (Art 113(a): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(6), as a provider of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the AI system developed for the sole purpose of scientific research and development` (Date 1 2 2025) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2 February 2025, specifically developed and put into service for research alone: JUST FALSE ("This Regulation does not apply to AI systems or AI models, including their output, specifically developed and put into service for the sole purpose of scientific research and development")
-- MIRROR Art 2(6): a provider and a deployer of an AI system developed for scientific research alone
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(6), as a provider of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the AI system developed for the sole purpose of scientific research and development` (Date 2 2 2025) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 2 February 2025, not for the sole purpose: NOTHING (limited by "for the sole purpose")
