§ `Article 3(1): is it an AI system?`

-- Under Article 3(1), as a provider of an AI system, is my software an AI system
-- all four elements met: TRUE ("a machine-based system that is designed to operate with varying levels of autonomy ... and that ... infers, from the input it receives, how to generate outputs ... that can influence physical or virtual environments")
-- MIRROR Art 3(1): the same software asked from the provider, deployer and person seats
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(1), as a provider of an AI system, is my software an AI system` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- not machine-based: FALSE (the definition says "means")
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(1), as a provider of an AI system, is my software an AI system` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- no autonomy: FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(1), as a provider of an AI system, is my software an AI system` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- does not infer how to generate outputs: FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(1), as a provider of an AI system, is my software an AI system` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- outputs cannot influence physical or virtual environments: FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(1), as a provider of an AI system, is my software an AI system` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE


§ `Article 3(3) to (8): does the definition of my role fit me?`

-- Under Article 3(3), as a provider of an AI system, does the definition of a provider fit me
-- develops it, places it on the market under its own name: TRUE ("develops an AI system or a general-purpose AI model ... and places it on the market ... under its own name or trademark")
-- MIRROR Art 3(3) and Art 3(7): a party that develops an AI system and places it under its own name is its provider, and so not its distributor
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(3), as a provider of an AI system, does the definition of a provider fit me` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- has it developed by someone else and places it under its own name: TRUE ("or that has an AI system or a general-purpose AI model developed")
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(3), as a provider of an AI system, does the definition of a provider fit me` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- develops it and has it developed, places it under its own name: TRUE
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(3), as a provider of an AI system, does the definition of a provider fit me` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- develops it but does not place it on the market: FALSE (the definition says "means")
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(3), as a provider of an AI system, does the definition of a provider fit me` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- develops it and places it, but not under its own name or trademark: FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(3), as a provider of an AI system, does the definition of a provider fit me` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- neither develops it nor has it developed: FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(3), as a provider of an AI system, does the definition of a provider fit me` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- Under Article 3(8), as a provider of an AI system, am I an operator
-- the seat's role is passed as the keel's `Role`: TRUE ("'operator' means a provider, product manufacturer, deployer, authorised representative, importer or distributor"): the role of this seat is on the list
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(8), as a provider of an AI system, am I an operator` EQUALS TRUE


§ `Article 3(9) to (11): placing on the market, making available on the market, putting into service`

-- Under Article 3(9), as a provider of an AI system, is my supply of the AI system a placing on the market
-- a first making available on the Union market: TRUE ("the first making available of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model on the Union market")
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(9), as a provider of an AI system, is my supply of the AI system a placing on the market` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- a making available that is not the first: FALSE (the definition says "means")
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(9), as a provider of an AI system, is my supply of the AI system a placing on the market` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- not a making available on the Union market: FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(9), as a provider of an AI system, is my supply of the AI system a placing on the market` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- Under Article 3(11), as a provider of an AI system, is my supply a putting into service
-- first use, directly to the deployer, for the intended purpose: TRUE
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(11), as a provider of an AI system, is my supply a putting into service` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- first use, for own use in the Union, for the intended purpose: TRUE ("directly to the deployer or for own use in the Union")
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(11), as a provider of an AI system, is my supply a putting into service` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- first use but neither directly to the deployer nor for own use: FALSE (the definition says "means")
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(11), as a provider of an AI system, is my supply a putting into service` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- not a supply for first use: FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(11), as a provider of an AI system, is my supply a putting into service` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- first use that is not for the intended purpose: FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(11), as a provider of an AI system, is my supply a putting into service` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE


