-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was `#ASSERT `Under Article 44(2), as a provider of an AI system, may the validity of a certificate be extended for a further period` (Date 1 9 2027) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE`; the Guide's In-short line gives JUST FALSE only for an if, only if, as long as, unless (or a plain variant) and the rulings of 2026-11-05 add where, when, upon: 'At the request of' is none of them, so NOTHING (ruling of 2026-11-12 in BRIEF.md; fork F-44-2-extension)
-- MIRROR pair-44-2
-- I have not requested the extension: a gate on a 'may' that is not where, when or upon.
