-- P6-cases-seat-provider: cases for the seat questions of P6-seat-provider (GENERATED by work/gen_seats.py).
-- Each case below is a layer-1 test of the function the question calls, with the same facts given through the seat's plain inputs; its expected value was decided from the text
-- before any run (the layer-1 tests P6-tests-*.l4 hold the reasoning). For the questions that take `the date asked`, it is the first argument; the role questions take no date.
-- A question has a case for each outcome its function can give: JUST TRUE ("yes"), JUST FALSE (the text says no) and NOTHING (not covered); a function that never says no (a bare "must", a grant) has none for JUST FALSE.
-- NOTES.md (Seats, P6) lists, per seat, which outcomes each question's cases assert. A case marked MIRROR is the same function and the same facts asked from the counterpart seat.

